95991b7852b855","changed":false,"changed_paths":[],"commit":"26bdc8c63747f14dc3c532c39b77992fb60cca73","commits":[],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","finding_commits":{},"parent":"26bdc8c63747f14dc3c532c39b77992fb60cca73","patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","tree":"c3f0a2ef2a3a906dbed7e684c53f7d62c8d85f5c"},"dispositions":{"comments":[{"body":"[P2] [General] Match the SDK service detector's entity schema\n\nWith declarative detectors ordered `manifest` then `service`, and `otel.service.name=demo` matching the manifest title, the detected `service.version` now disappears. SDK 1.67.0's `ServiceResourceDetector` gives its `service` entity schema URL `https://opentelemetry.io/schemas/1.40.0`, whereas this entity has no schema URL. `ResourceBuilder` merges descriptions only when both the identifying attributes and entity schema URLs match, so it replaces the manifest entity wholesale, dropping its version even though the service name is unchanged. I reproduced this with the real detectors: the pre-PR resource retains `service.version=1.0`, the new resource loses it, and matching entity schemas preserves it. Align the service entity schema with the SDK detector and cover this composition in a regression test.","line":33,"path":"instrumentation/resources/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/resources/internal/ServiceResource.java","side":"RIGHT"}],"input_identity":{"pr_diff_sha256":"11ac0711aa039e59b5f32c0658ed3970b110451f561bbfd5c5b3158563f3d570"},"outcome":"comments","request_digest":"ed0773bfd6cebfb4bb8847590f9b48624675fc92d8deada7e5f9a2920b8dae43","schema":2},"download_sha256":"96518b52a84e7251d1d24715a3453e77b11c8955368cfdd9828e23801bdc9c82","frozen_sha":"26bdc8c63747f14dc3c532c39b77992fb60cca73","pr":20632,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"ed0773bfd6cebfb4bb8847590f9b4862467